From: Zurker <47176362+XIAO1287643931@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 07:05:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Papo: prefetch join reads during the login RTT window

The join flow reads playerdata (.dat gzip+NBT+datafix), stats JSON and
advancements JSON synchronously on the main thread. The final GameProfile is
resolved well before those reads (at least one client RTT earlier), so batch 82
issues the reads onto the per-target ordered write chains in that window:

- PlayerDataStorage: pure-read/pure-fix prefetch body (readCompressed +
  MCDataConverter.convertTag, both already concurrency-proven via moonrise
  workers); the .offline-read rename and _corrupted_ backup side effects stay
  at the consume point so an aborted login can never leave them behind
- PlayerList: stats/advancements strict-JSON prefetch keyed by resolved path,
  consume-once take + disconnect discard hooks
- login/configuration listeners: trigger at startClientVerification (all auth
  modes converge there), discard on disconnect
- reads run at Priority.BLOCKING (the priority vanilla sync-loads use), so a
  saturated IO pool still schedules the main-thread join ahead of queued
  region IO

Fallback: no prefetch / pool halted / body failure -> original synchronous
path byte-for-byte unchanged.

